From 86a1787a5df6362490930d9761daec1fc1d56f29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 06:08:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 506/638] content: quarantine retiring AROS renderers

Treat channel error and fast shutdown as one idempotent renderer-retirement transition. A timeout requests termination but never authorizes replacement; the host continues polling until the Exec child task is independently gone and its Mojo reader and ports have fully retired.

This prevents latency during failure cleanup from accumulating replacement children, reader tasks, and retained channel memory.



